# Oshiire configuration. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values.
#
# ############################################################################
# #  WARNING -- `.env` CARRIES TWO SECRETS. NEVER COMMIT OR SHARE IT.        #
# #                                                                          #
# #  REDDIT_SAVED_FEED_URL contains a per-account access token. Anyone who   #
# #  has that URL can read your entire saved list without logging in.        #
# #                                                                          #
# #  REDDIT_SESSION_COOKIE is a logged-in browser cookie. Anyone who has it  #
# #  IS you on Reddit -- it is the more dangerous of the two by a wide       #
# #  margin, because it is not read-only and is not limited to your saves.   #
# #                                                                          #
# #  Treat both exactly like passwords: do not commit them, do not paste     #
# #  them into an issue, a chat, a screenshot, or a bug report, and do not   #
# #  let them into a log file.                                               #
# #                                                                          #
# #  `.env` is gitignored, and this file (`.env.example`) is the only one    #
# #  of the pair that is committed -- keep it that way, and keep both        #
# #  values below EMPTY.                                                     #
# #                                                                          #
# #  If either does leak: change your Reddit password. That invalidates the  #
# #  feed URL and the session cookie together (and is also why both stop     #
# #  working after any password change -- you then re-copy them).            #
# ############################################################################

# Your private Reddit saved-posts RSS feed.
#
# Where to find it: log in to Reddit, go to https://old.reddit.com/prefs/feeds/
# and copy the RSS link next to "your saved links". Reddit hands it to you on
# the `old.reddit.com` host; change that to `www.reddit.com` and keep
# everything from `/saved.rss?` onward exactly as copied, so the value you
# paste below looks like
#   https://www.reddit.com/saved.rss?feed=<64-hex-token>&user=<your-username>
# The `feed=` parameter is the secret token.
#
# Why the host swap: since the end of July 2026 `old.reddit.com` answers its
# logged-out endpoints with a login page instead of the content, so the
# old.reddit form of this URL returns the login wall rather than your saves.
# (Ingest rewrites an old.reddit feed host to www for you, but paste the www
# form anyway -- it is what actually gets used.)
#
# The feed returns roughly your 25 most recent saves. Appending `&limit=100`
# widens that to ~100, which is the practical maximum -- there is no
# pagination, so anything older than the window is unreachable from the feed.
# (Getting at older saves is what the backfill subsystem is for; see
# docs/BACKFILL.md.)
#
# This feed is READ-ONLY. Oshiire cannot unsave, vote, or write anything back
# to your account through it.
REDDIT_SAVED_FEED_URL=

# The root folder of your sorted archive -- where approved images are filed.
#
# It does NOT have to be an existing, organized archive: point it at an empty
# folder and the first `--apply` run creates the subfolders it needs. It can be
# a cloud-synced folder (Google Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox); Oshiire only ever
# moves files into it and lets the sync client do the upload. Use an absolute
# path. On Windows, either forward slashes or doubled backslashes are fine:
#   ARCHIVE_DIR=C:/Users/you/Google Drive/Art
ARCHIVE_DIR=

# Optional. Included in the User-Agent header of every request to Reddit, per
# Reddit's API etiquette guidelines, so a human is identifiable if a request
# pattern ever looks wrong. Not a secret -- it is your public username. Leave
# it blank to send a generic, non-identifying value instead.
REDDIT_USERNAME=

# Optional, and a SECRET when set -- more dangerous than the feed URL above.
#
# A logged-in cookie string copied from your browser. Get it from devtools ->
# Network -> click any request to old.reddit.com while logged in -> Headers ->
# Request Headers -> copy the whole `Cookie:` value. Paste it as one line:
#   REDDIT_SESSION_COOKIE=reddit_session=<value>; token_v2=<value>; ...
# (The devtools Application/Storage -> Cookies view works too, but the Network
# tab gives you the exact string the browser is actually sending.)
#
# Why it is needed: at the end of July 2026 old.reddit.com started requiring
# login for its logged-out HTML endpoints. Three parts of Oshiire read
# old.reddit HTML -- ingest's gallery permalink fetch, the backfill CSV sweep,
# and calibrate.py -- and without this cookie all three receive the login wall
# instead of the page they asked for. The RSS feed above does NOT need it; it
# is read from www.reddit.com with no cookie at all. Leave this blank if you
# only ingest single-image posts from the feed.
#
# The cookie is necessary but not sufficient: those fetches also go out over
# curl_cffi's Chrome-impersonated transport (installed by requirements.txt),
# because plain `requests` hits the wall carrying this exact cookie. You do not
# have to configure that part -- just be aware the cookie alone is not the
# whole trick.
#
# Anyone holding this value is logged in as you, with far more reach than the
# read-only feed token. Do not commit it. It expires: re-copy it from the
# browser after any password change or logout, and whenever a run stops with
# "Reddit returned its login wall".
REDDIT_SESSION_COOKIE=
